<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104136" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τμήγω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Nic.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			72
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			D.P.
			1043
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Man.
			2.75
		</span></i>: fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τμήξω </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-</span>)
			<i><span class="en">
			Parm.
			2
		</span></i>: aor. 1
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτμηξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(2).473
				</span></i>
			 (Megalop., <span class="entity">iii A.D.</span>); 
				Dor.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτμᾱξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					8.24
				</span></i>
			 (prob.): aor. 2
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι-έτμᾰγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.276
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτμηξάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.480
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>):—
				Pass.
			, aor. 2
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτμάγην [ᾰ</span>] in 
				Ep.
			
			3pl.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τμάγεν</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διατμήγω</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.374
			</span></i>; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτμήγην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					300
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.661
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i>): more freq. in comp. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά</span>:—
				Ep.
			 collat. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέμνω</span>,
				<i>cut, cleave</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σικύας,
			πυετίην</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
			</span></i> ll. cc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλαμος [δάκτυλον]
				ἔτμαξεν</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> l.c.; <i>cut</i>, of a circle, <i><span class="en">
				Man.
			</span></i> l.c.:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδὸν ἐτμήξαντο</span>
			<i>cut their</i> way, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7
			</span></i>.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.
			in aor. 2
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be divided</i> or <i>dispersed, part</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ ἂρ τμάγεν</span>
		Il.l.c.</div>
